      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brooklyn%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s motto, “Founded by Chance, Sustained by Courage,” reflects its resilient history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brooklyn%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Quinn Chapel AME, established in 1838, served as an Underground Railroad station, sheltering escaping slaves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brooklyn%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2007, residents founded the Historical Society of Brooklyn, Illinois, to preserve the town’s rich past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
